WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.366
- [Kelly] Our next guest
is a comedian, actress

00:00:02.366 --> 00:00:05.300
and the host of her very
own late night talk show.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.650
It's amazing, you gotta check it out.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.210
From NBC's "A Little
Late With Lilly Singh",

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.119
please welcome Lilly Singh.

00:00:11.119 --> 00:00:13.702
(upbeat music)

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.940
It's great to see you. Where are you?

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.120
I love wherever, wherever
you're at! Where are you?

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.310
- [Lilly] So, thank you
so much for having me.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.530
I'm so happy to see your face.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:24.300
I am in my set house,
which is my fun house

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.670
where I'm shooting season two

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.120
of "A Little Late With Lilly
Singh", so not my real house-

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.789
a rented house that I won't be upset about

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:33.930
if the walls get dinged
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:34.763
- [Kelly] You haven't been to my house,

00:00:34.763 --> 00:00:38.148
you'd find another house,
um, so it looks great!

00:00:38.148 --> 00:00:41.320
I love your vibe. I love well, obviously,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.320
I love color as well, but
you're always so colorful

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.390
and so bright. Like, I
feel like I could be having

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.500
the worst day ever, and
I see you, and I smile.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.900
You're like that person,
yeah, I love that about you.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.510
And you did an interview
recently that caught my eye

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.730
because check this out everybody.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.580
- [Lilly] Oh yeah.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.280
- [Kelly] That sunflower jumpsuit,

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:03.249
what's happening, and where do I get one?

00:01:03.249 --> 00:01:05.630
- [Lilly] I'm gonna text
you all the details,

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.560
but I did learn that sunflowers

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.150
and clearly you have some
there are your favorite flower.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.330
And here's the thing I'm so bummed, Kelly,

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.280
because, you know, we can't
be doing this in person,

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.510
we have to be doing this over zoom,

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.040
but that didn't stop me
from getting you flowers

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.882
that I could give you virtually.

00:01:17.882 --> 00:01:19.410
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.520
- I will- I will just
take them home for myself,

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.680
but they're for you!
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.527
- [Kelly] So it's a gift for everyone.

00:01:25.527 --> 00:01:28.688
Well, you and I, you
and I text often about

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.822
the talk show stuff and especially,

00:01:30.822 --> 00:01:33.640
I mean, right when both of
us started our talk shows

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.765
the world like shut down.
- [Lilly] Yep.

00:01:35.765 --> 00:01:38.168
- [Kelly] So, I know we
both keep going, you know,

00:01:38.168 --> 00:01:39.800
back and forth about, "Wait, what are you-

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:40.980
what can you do? what can you do?"

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.160
'Cause it's like the weirdest thing

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.910
to shoot a show right now.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:47.203
But I love how authentic you
insist on being in your show.

00:01:47.203 --> 00:01:49.740
It's just that you're,
is that something you've

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.650
always been like since you were a kid?

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.280
- [Lilly] Thank you! Well, this
is the best interview ever.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.490
Keep the compliments
coming, Kelly, my God!

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.440
Honestly, it's something that I worked on.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.620
You know, when I made
my first YouTube videos,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.930
I was uncomfortable, and then
I learned to get to a place

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.770
to be myself and when
I started "Late Night",

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.660
I had to go through that
journey all over again.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.140
Like, admittedly, in season one,

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.240
I thought there was moments

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:12.110
where I wasn't completely being myself.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.070
Maybe I was nervous or I
felt a lot of pressure,

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.230
and, so, with season two,
I'm really prioritizing

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.750
throwing all facades out the window,

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.180
I wanna be completely authentic.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.704
You know, me and my producers always have

00:02:21.704 --> 00:02:23.550
little mini headbutt sessions,

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.550
because I'll be interviewing a guest

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:26.927
and they'll script something that's like,

00:02:26.927 --> 00:02:28.400
"You know, I love doing this movie,"

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.250
and I'll be like, "I've
never seen that movie."

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.510
And I insist on being authentic about it,

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:33.750
because I don't wanna lie.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.920
I'd rather make the time
to watch all of the things

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.720
before I interview someone

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.650
and if I don't have the time,

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:39.977
I'd rather be honest and say like,

00:02:39.977 --> 00:02:42.590
"Listen, people online are
going crazy about you,"

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:45.970
as opposed to like, "I
loved you in this movie

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.020
and I'm such a big fan,"

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.864
because it just feels like
it doesn't sound real.

00:02:49.864 --> 00:02:53.080
Putting on a facade and
putting on a face and lying,

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.440
it's exhausting.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.000
It's so much more fun to
just be real and be yourself.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.720
Yes, it's a little more scary,

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.820
but I just feel like I'm in
such a good place right now

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.390
where I'm so weird and
I show it on my show

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.500
and I have nothing to hide.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.780
I'm just like, "This weirdo is who you get

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:09.650
and you're not gonna get anybody else."

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.440
- [Kelly] I think we're
all a little weird,

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.810
I think that's why people love you.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:13.643
Like, we're all a little weird

00:03:13.643 --> 00:03:15.600
and I don't think that's abnormal.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.690
- [Lilly] Me and you,
specifically, are super weird.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.001
- [Kelly] Yeah, we might be
at the end of the spectrum,

00:03:20.001 --> 00:03:21.510
(Kelly laughs)
that's fine,

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.220
it's working out for us.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.910
But wait, I wanna ask you about this,

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:26.420
because you've actually
been working with OLAY,

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.186
and so can you tell us
about their new campaign

00:03:28.186 --> 00:03:29.970
and the OLAY skin promise?

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.120
- [Lilly] For sure. I actually love this,

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.370
and it's one of the many reasons
I love working with OLAY.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.570
The OLAY skin promise is a commitment

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:39.110
to not retouching my
skin in advertisements.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.000
And they're the first
mass brand skincare line

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:42.880
to do this in the US.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.210
And so this has also helped
with my authenticity,

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.760
because it's like my blemishes,

00:03:47.628 --> 00:03:48.828
my pimples don't get retouched.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.320
It's me being proud in the skin I'm in.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.793
- [Kelly] Yeah, I love that!

00:03:52.725 --> 00:03:54.380
And do you have a favorite OLAY products?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.730
I'm like really into skincare,

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:00.220
because I have like hormonal acne, so.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.280
- [Lilly] Oh, yeah, I do
have a favorite product.

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:03.590
I mean, I love a lot of their products,

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.300
but here's the deal, Kelly,
I'm gonna be real with you.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.780
I have to leave my house
to go to set at 7:30 AM.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.313
So, obviously, I set my
alarm for 7:15 AM and then I-

00:04:12.313 --> 00:04:13.399
- [Kelly] We're the same.

00:04:13.399 --> 00:04:15.360
- [Lilly] You think I'm
doing this as a joke,

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.500
but this is one hundred percent accurate.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.080
I hit snooze once, but I
wake up at seven-twenty.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:21.360
So, now I have 10 minutes
to get into my car,

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.190
and, literally, I brush my teeth.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.760
I start with my OLAY Collagen
Peptide 24 moisturizer.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.220
Absorbs quickly, it's
not sticky or greasy.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.290
It hydrates my skin for 24
hours, which I super need,

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.300
and I just have firmer looking
skin and in like two weeks.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.910
So, my skin has been popping
in season two, just saying.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.640
- [Kelly] All right, well,
good news for everyone

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.410
in the house seats today;
you are all getting

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.241
a $50 CVS gift card, so you can all

00:04:43.241 --> 00:04:45.849
try Lilly's favorite OLAY moisturizer,

00:04:45.849 --> 00:04:49.790
and for you all at home, if
you spend $50 on OLAY products

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:54.450
at CVS or CVS.com, you'll
also get a $15 mail-in rebate.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:56.525
So a deal is a deal, and it's amazing.

00:04:56.525 --> 00:04:59.320
Thank you so much, Lilly!
I love you so much!

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.360
- [Lilly] Thank you! I love you, too.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.377
- [Kelly] Good luck, good luck.

00:05:02.377 --> 00:05:04.560
"A little late with Lilly Singh" is on NBC

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:07.351
at 1:35 AM Eastern and 12:25 AM central.

00:05:07.351 --> 00:05:09.701
Y'all got to check the
show out; she's amazing.

